# Complex Learn Backend

Node.js + Express + MongoDB/Mongoose API scaffold.

## Setup
1. Install Node.js (LTS).
2. In this folder run `npm install`.
3. Copy `.env.example` to `.env`.
4. Set `MONGO_URI` and a long random `JWT_SECRET`.
5. Run `npm run dev`.

API default: http://localhost:5000
Health: GET `/api/health`

## Routes
- POST `/api/auth/register` — student registration
- POST `/api/auth/login` — student or teacher login (`role` required)
- GET `/api/auth/me` — current account (Bearer token)
- GET `/api/students/dashboard` — student dashboard
- GET `/api/teachers/dashboard` — teacher dashboard
- GET `/api/teachers/students` — teacher student list
- GET `/api/tests` — published tests (Bearer token)
- POST `/api/tests` — teacher creates test
- PATCH `/api/tests/:id/publish` — teacher publishes own test
- POST `/api/tests/:id/submit` — student submits answers
- GET `/api/results` — student own results or teacher results
- GET `/api/rewards` — student's reward history
- GET/POST `/api/materials` — list/upload material metadata
- GET/POST `/api/timetable` — student timetable
- GET/POST `/api/reminders` — student reminders
- POST `/api/ai/ask` — AI placeholder (501 until provider integration)

## Important
- `.env` must never be committed or shared.
- `fileUrl` is metadata only; implement secure file storage before allowing uploads.
- AI endpoint is deliberately not connected to a provider yet.
- For production, add rate limiting, validation, email verification, password reset,
  audit logs, pagination, and stronger test/reward abuse prevention.
- The demo coin rule awards 5 coins for >=80% test score; adjust to your project rules.
